5) at -225: the algo gave it 65% vs 66% fair (-1 pts) — lost (-1u); lost to the close (closing fair chance 66%). LAC ML (+185) at +185: the algo gave it 35% vs 34% fair (+1 pts) — won (+1.9u); lost to the close (closing fair chance 34%). BAL -4.5 (-112) at -112: the algo gave it 49% vs 50% fair (-1.1 pts) — lost (-1u); lost to the closing -3.5 by 1. LAC +4.5 (-108) at -108: the algo gave it 51% vs 50% fair (+1.1 pts) — won (+0.9u); beat the closing +3.5 by 1. OVER 39.5 (-108) at -108: the algo gave it 50% vs 50% fair (+0.6 pts) — won (+0.9u); same number as the close. UNDER 39.5 (-112) at -112: the algo gave it 50% vs 50% fair (-0.6 pts) — lost (-1u); same number as the close.\n\nFrom the algo's snapshot to the close: spread Ravens -4.5 → -3.5.\n\nNo bet: nothing cleared the algo's bar before the game."},{"title":"Where the public and the money were","body":"Splits (Action Network): spread: 51% of bets on Chargers, 46% of the money — Chargers covered; total: 69% of bets on the over, 74% of the money — it went over; moneyline: 18% of bets on Chargers, 46% of the money.\n\nThe sharp side by the algo's read was Ravens, who lost and didn't cover."},{"title":"What the algo learns","body":"This game's own lesson: scoring came in at ×1.022 of the raw projection, and the home side beat its projected margin by -6 points. It counts toward NFL scoring level, home edge and both teams' attack and defense corrections.\n\nAcross 29 graded NFL games the algo now scales scoring ×0.983 and gives home teams -1.1 points. Team corrections start after 3 graded games for a team."},{"title":"Bottom line","body":"Wrong side, total within its normal range, margin within its normal range, no bet."}],"archived":"2026-11-17T04:26:13.162Z"}}}